  "contracts": {
    "tick": "Flow+0xc generation is an 8-bit increment, including wrap to zero. Nodes are scanned in array order. Active bit0 or monitor bit0x100 enters processing if node generation differs. Successful activation sets0x802 and clears bit0, then recursively activates children. Condition parents may revisit an already stamped child.",
    "timer": "Gizmo activation finishes immediately, but output remains false until enabled flag bit0 and remaining<=0. Update subtracts delta when remaining>=0; it does not clamp negative results. Activate/deactivate both reset duration, with randomized reset when flag bit1 is set.",
    "loopReset": "Recursive0x59da60 stamps byte+9, stops at owning Loop and previously visited generation. It deactivates descendant gizmos unless nodeflag0x1000 is set; it does not clear node completion flags. A fresh reset generation is used for each immediate Loop child.",
    "parentCleanup": "Pending flag0x20 releases when all children cross their state barrier: ordinary children may be inactive or the current child; children with flags0xc0 require completion and no0x100. Flag0x10 deactivates associated gizmos if flag8 is absent; flag0x40 clears0x100 and recursively releases parents. Reverse callback behavior itself remains unverified.",
    "cycleCount": "0x59da30 uses custom EDI root and returns reachable root-return edge count for loop startup threshold adjustment.",
    "monitor": "Condition output with flag0x200 recomputes its kind process with temporary flag0x400, then restores the prior flag0x400 value. Without monitor it returns completion bit1.",
    "TurnOnFlowBox": "Case-insensitive matching of all node names. name= chooses target; FALSE disables active bit0. TRUE does not undo FALSE within a call. Other flags/completion remain unchanged. Linked actions run in order.",
    "GizRandom": "16-bit QRAND is state=(state*0x24cd+1)&65535. Draw=1+floor(updatedState*C*100), where C is the exact binary64 reciprocal at0x751700, evaluated by x87 before truncation. Its slight rounding below1/65535 keeps the top draw at100. Select the first inclusive cumulative interval. All65536 states give exactly16384 choices per output for25/25/25/25 weights."
  },
  "limits": [
    "Graph DAG scheduling model covers action/condition nodes and timer callbacks, not every gizmo or arbitrary cyclic scheduler graph.",
    "A Timer/Action/Loop cycle, including actual initialization, was checked for270 frames at each of four durations, including generation wrap. Other real puzzle topologies and non-timer gizmos remain unverified.",
    "Reset/monitor side effects on real non-timer gizmos remain unverified.",
